  clock: 4  # 4b18
  nonce: 4b18  # 4b18
  message: "Fixed in PR #1789 (dev 43531aa877). ROOT CAUSE: the walk's per-line call index (_WalkIndexes.callee_names) held only calls with a catalogue key, so an unresolved acc.push / acc.append (and any resolved first-party call) was absent and the use line read as 'no call at this line at all', the permitting case that skips the escape question. Same hole on the no-heir branch (log(acc.push(t)) read as all-terminating). FIX: a taint call edge with no key adds UNCATALOGUED_CALL at its sites; no summary is keyed by it, so it never closes a branch (the _source_line_escapes rule, now on every line); covers all four walk sites. BEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, the filed repro re-run on merged dev with the shipped CLI (verify-claims, host_secret -> network): JS n = acc.push(t) ... fetch(url + acc[0]) -> violated [env -> fetch, ddg_mixed/escaped] (was confirmed_with_caveats); Python n = acc.append(t) ... sock.sendall(acc[0].encode()) -> violated [environ -> sendall, ddg_mixed/escaped]; the no-heir control unchanged (violated). Tests: test_taint_use_line_calls.py (4 red before the fix, control green). Corpus A/B (flask-restful, gin, coredns, Tone.js, fastapi, buildah, dash.js, django): 0 verdicts / 0 evidence tuples moved; an uncapped census of every walk call moved 0 of 3538 results (False occurs once in that corpus, no uncatalogued use-line call). NOT MEASURED: Go/Java/C/Rust fixtures of this shape. Follow-up: re-test relaxing WI-tozar's CONTAINED ONLY rule. Notebook: notebookjournal_10212026_tinav.md."  # 4b18
