  message: "FOLLOW-UP MERGED, PR #1790 (dev e926fc1045): WI-tozar's CONTAINED ONLY rule removed. A Python walrus / JS-TS nested assignment now defines its target wherever its value also goes (call argument, receiver, return, container); still weak where it may not run, still a use inside a closure. Its only reason was the walk hole WI-tinav closed (PR #1789). Evidence on merged dev, shipped CLI: the two consequence guards (escape at the binding's own line and on a later use line, Python + JS) stay violated with the binding defined; JS acc.push(k = t) ... fetch(url + acc[0]) -> violated [env -> fetch, ddg_mixed/escaped]. Corpus vs merged dev (flask-restful, Tone.js, fastapi, dash.js, django; 7 claims): 0 verdicts, 0 evidence tuples, 0 of 554 walk results moved. Notebook: notebookjournal_10212026_tinav.md."  # 2511
